message: "Please cite the exact public commit or archival release of this disclosure."
title: "The proper hat-guessing number of K7-e"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Protti"
    given-names: "Matthew"
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-09-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthewprotti/proper-hat-guessing-k5-minus-e/tree/k7e-v0.1-reviewed/research/proper_hat_guessing_k7_minus_e"
abstract: >-
  We prove that the proper hat-guessing number of the complete graph on seven
  vertices with one edge removed is twelve. Two explicit lower-bound proofs
  use disjoint Witt designs and a sharply five-transitive twelve-point orbit
  construction, completed by a common Hall criterion.
keywords:
  - hat guessing
  - proper coloring
  - graph theory
  - Hall's theorem
  - Steiner systems
  - permutation groups
  - AI-assisted mathematics
